{
  "tema": 5267,
  "slug": "he-hablado-perfecto-ar",
  "titulo": "Regular -ar verbs in the present perfect",
  "subtitulo": "He trabajado mucho esta semana.",
  "foto": "t03.jpg",
  "regla": "The present perfect is haber in the present (he, has, ha, hemos, han) + the participle. For -ar verbs, the participle swaps -ar for -ado: hablar → he hablado.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The present perfect (**pretérito perfecto**) has two parts: **haber** in the present + the **past participle**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "For **-ar** verbs, drop **-ar** and add **-ado**: **hablar → hablado**, **trabajar → trabajado**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "he / has / ha / hemos / han",
            "+ stem +",
            "-ado"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "haber",
            "+ participle"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "**he**",
              "hablado"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "**has**",
              "hablado"
            ],
            [
              "él / ella / usted",
              "**ha**",
              "hablado"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros",
              "**hemos**",
              "hablado"
            ],
            [
              "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
              "**han**",
              "hablado"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Only **haber** changes. The participle **never changes**: **ella ha llegado**, **ellas han llegado**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "The two parts stay together. **No** and pronouns go **before haber**: **no lo he terminado**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In Mexico it's used for experiences (**nunca he viajado**) and for periods that aren't over (**esta semana**, **hoy**). For a finished recent action, Mexicans prefer the preterite: **¿Ya cenaste?**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==He trabajado== mucho esta semana.",
              "en": "I've worked a lot this week."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Has probado== los tacos de birria de la esquina?",
              "en": "Have you tried the birria tacos on the corner?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi hermana nunca ==ha viajado== a Oaxaca.",
              "en": "My sister has never traveled to Oaxaca."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Hemos entrenado== tres veces esta semana.",
              "en": "We've trained three times this week."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los vecinos ==han plantado== jitomates en el patio.",
              "en": "The neighbors have planted tomatoes in the yard."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿Ustedes ==han surfeado== en Ensenada?",
              "en": "Have you guys surfed in Ensenada?"
            },
            {
              "es": "Todavía no ==he terminado== el capítulo.",
              "en": "I haven't finished the chapter yet."
            },
            {
              "es": "Nunca me ==he enojado== con ella.",
              "en": "I've never gotten mad at her."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "He hablo con él."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "He hablado con él."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Use the participle in **-ado**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Yo ha trabajado hoy."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Yo he trabajado hoy."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "**Yo he**, not **yo ha**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "He ya terminado."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Ya he terminado."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Nothing goes between **he** and the participle."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Ellas han llegadas."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Ellas han llegado."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "The participle doesn't agree."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
